    fullDescriptionEn: "Accessibility (a11y, short for \"a\" + 11 letters + \"y\") means designing websites with the needs of people with disabilities in mind: low vision, hearing impairments, motor impairments.\n\nStandard: WCAG 2.1 (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines). Levels: A (minimum), AA (standard), AAA (highest).\n\nAccessibility fundamentals: proper semantic HTML markup, ARIA attributes, sufficient colour contrast (4.5:1 for text), keyboard navigation support (Tab), alt tags for images.\n\nCodeworth runs 43+ axe accessibility tests on every project.",
