    fullDescriptionEn: "The term \"Foundation Model\" was introduced by Stanford HAI in 2021. These models radically changed AI: instead of training a separate model for every task, you adapt one large model.\n\n**Key characteristics:**\n\n**Scale:**\n- GPT-4: ~1.8 trillion parameters (estimated)\n- Llama 3 70B: 70 billion parameters\n- Claude 3.5 Sonnet: ~200B+ parameters (estimated)\n- Gemini 1.5 Pro: ~1T+ parameters (estimated)\n\n**Training:**\n- Pretrained on trillions of tokens from the internet, books, code, and academic papers\n- Unsupervised / self-supervised: next-token prediction (GPT) or masked language modelling (BERT)\n- Compute: thousands of A100/H100 GPU-months, costing $10M–$100M+\n\n**Foundation model categories:**\n- **Text:** GPT-4o, Claude 3.5, Llama 3, Gemini 1.5, Mistral Large\n- **Code:** GitHub Copilot (GPT-4), Claude, Gemini Code\n- **Image:** DALL-E 3, Stable Diffusion 3, Midjourney v6, Flux\n- **Multimodal:** GPT-4o Vision, Gemini 1.5 Pro, Claude 3.5 (text + images)\n- **Audio:** Whisper (STT), ElevenLabs (TTS), Suno (music)\n- **Video:** Sora (OpenAI), Runway Gen-3, Kling\n\n**Adaptation methods:**\n1. **Zero-shot:** used without any customisation\n2. **Few-shot prompting:** examples supplied in the context window\n3. **Fine-tuning:** additional training on domain-specific data\n4. **LoRA / QLoRA:** parameter-efficient fine-tuning\n5. **RAG:** augmenting with external knowledge\n\n**UK market:**\n- AWS Bedrock: Claude, Llama, Titan API\n- Azure OpenAI: GPT-4o, Embeddings (popular with UK enterprise)\n- Google Vertex AI: Gemini, PaLM",
