    shortDescriptionEn: "AI systems that process several types of input simultaneously (text + images + audio + video). Examples: GPT-4o Vision, Gemini 1.5 Pro, Claude 3.5 — unlocking new classes of business applications.",
    fullDescriptionEn: "Multimodal AI removes a key limitation of early LLMs — working with text alone. Modern systems \"understand\" several modalities at once.\n\n**Current state (2025–2026):**\n\n**Text + Image (Vision):**\n- GPT-4o: analysis of images, charts, documents, screenshots\n- Claude 3.5 Sonnet: document understanding, diagram analysis\n- Gemini 1.5 Pro: up to 1M token context + images\n\n**Text + Audio:**\n- GPT-4o Audio: real-time voice conversation with emotional awareness\n- Whisper + GPT-4: an STT → text analysis pipeline\n- ElevenLabs: text → natural speech (100+ languages)\n\n**Text + Video:**\n- Gemini 1.5 Pro: video up to one hour long in the context window\n- GPT-4o Video (2025): frame-by-frame video understanding\n\n**Image + Text Generation:**\n- DALL-E 3: text prompt → image\n- Stable Diffusion 3: open source, local deployment\n- Flux 1.1: state-of-the-art quality (2024–2025)\n\n**Architectural approaches:**\n- **Cross-attention fusion:** separate encoders per modality plus a cross-attention layer\n- **Unified tokenization:** images are tokenised as patches (ViT), audio as spectrograms\n- **CLIP-based alignment:** linking visual and text representations in a shared space\n\n**UK business applications:**\n- Insurance: automatic damage assessment from car accident photos\n- NHS: analysis of medical images (X-ray, MRI) combined with clinical notes\n- Retail: visual product search plus text description\n- Legal: analysis of scanned documents and handwritten contracts",
