    slug: "buyout-readiness-ml",
    termUk: "ML-оцінка готовності до баяуту (buyout)",
    termEn: "ML Scoring for Pension Buyout Readiness",
    category: "data",
    shortDescription: "Machine learning models that assess how prepared a defined benefit pension scheme is to transact a buyout or buy-in with an insurer — scoring data quality, funding level, and pricing attractiveness.",
    fullDescription: "A pension buyout transfers a DB scheme's liabilities to a regulated insurer (a bulk purchase annuity), discharging the sponsor's obligation entirely; a buy-in is a partial version held as a scheme asset. With UK DB funding levels strengthened by higher gilt yields since 2022, the bulk annuity market has grown rapidly (multi-tens of billions of pounds annually), and many schemes are racing to assess buyout readiness.\n\nBuyout readiness has several dimensions: (1) funding sufficiency — does the scheme have enough assets to meet insurer pricing, which is more conservative than ongoing funding? (2) data quality — are member records (dates of birth, benefit structures, spouse details, GMP equalisation) clean enough for an insurer to underwrite? (3) investment alignment — are assets in a form insurers will accept in-specie? (4) timing — when will insurer pricing be most favourable given capacity?\n\nWhere ML helps: machine learning models score readiness by (a) detecting member-data anomalies and missing-field patterns that would inflate insurer data-load pricing, (b) predicting insurer quote levels from historical transaction data and current credit/longevity spreads, (c) optimising the de-risking glide path to a buyout target, and (d) classifying schemes by transaction feasibility windows.\n\nUK context: advisers (LCP, Aon, WTW) and insurers (PIC, L&G, Rothesay, Aviva, Standard Life) dominate this market. Codeworth builds data-readiness scoring pipelines that flag and remediate member-data issues before they reach an insurer.",
    shortDescriptionEn: "Machine learning models that assess how prepared a defined benefit pension scheme is to transact a buyout or buy-in with an insurer — scoring data quality, funding level, and pricing attractiveness.",
