    slug: "semantic-segmentation-cv",
    termUk: "Семантична сегментація (DeepLab/SegFormer)",
    termEn: "Semantic Segmentation (DeepLab/SegFormer)",
    category: "ai",
    shortDescription: "A computer-vision task that classifies every pixel in an image into a category, producing dense per-pixel labels — implemented by architectures such as DeepLabv3+ and the transformer-based SegFormer.",
    fullDescription: "Semantic segmentation assigns a class label to every pixel in an image (road, building, person, defect, tissue), in contrast to image classification (one label per image) or object detection (bounding boxes). The output is a dense segmentation map the same resolution as the input, enabling precise scene understanding.\n\nKey architectures: Fully Convolutional Networks (FCN) pioneered end-to-end pixel labelling. U-Net introduced an encoder-decoder with skip connections, dominant in medical imaging. The DeepLab family (DeepLabv3+) uses atrous (dilated) convolutions and atrous spatial pyramid pooling (ASPP) to capture multi-scale context without losing resolution. SegFormer (2021) replaced convolutional backbones with a hierarchical Vision Transformer encoder plus a lightweight all-MLP decoder, achieving strong accuracy-efficiency trade-offs. The Segment Anything Model (SAM) later generalised promptable segmentation.\n\nEvaluation: performance is measured by mean Intersection-over-Union (mIoU) and pixel accuracy across classes.\n\nWhere it adds business value: manufacturing defect mapping (exact defect area, not just presence), medical imaging (tumour and organ delineation), satellite/aerial analytics (land use, crop health), retail (shelf and product mapping), and autonomous systems.\n\nUK context: applications include NHS radiology segmentation, precision-agriculture crop monitoring, infrastructure inspection (rail, bridges), and quality control in advanced manufacturing. Codeworth builds segmentation pipelines (DeepLabv3+ / SegFormer, fine-tuned on client data) with mIoU reporting and edge-deployable variants for on-site inspection.",
    shortDescriptionEn: "A computer-vision task that classifies every pixel in an image into a category, producing dense per-pixel labels — implemented by architectures such as DeepLabv3+ and the transformer-based SegFormer.",
