    slug: "feature-store-platform",
    termUk: "Платформа feature store (Feast/Tecton)",
    termEn: "Feature Store Platform (Feast/Tecton)",
    category: "mlops",
    shortDescription: "A centralised platform for defining, storing, serving, and reusing machine learning features consistently across training and real-time inference — exemplified by Feast and Tecton.",
    fullDescription: "A feature store is the data layer of MLOps: it manages the engineered features that models consume, providing a single source of truth so the same feature definitions are used in both training and serving. This solves the notorious training-serving skew problem, where features computed differently in batch (for training) versus online (for live inference) silently degrade model accuracy.\n\nCore components: an offline store (historical feature values for training, typically a data warehouse / lake — BigQuery, Snowflake, S3/Parquet) and an online store (low-latency lookup for real-time inference — Redis, DynamoDB, Cassandra), kept consistent. Crucially, feature stores provide point-in-time correct joins to assemble training datasets without label leakage (using only feature values that were known at each event's timestamp), plus a feature registry for discovery, versioning, lineage, and reuse across teams.\n\nKey platforms: Feast is the leading open-source feature store (lightweight, bring-your-own infrastructure). Tecton is a managed, enterprise platform (founded by the creators of Uber's Michelangelo) that also handles feature transformation pipelines and streaming. Cloud-native options include Databricks Feature Store, SageMaker Feature Store, and Vertex AI Feature Store.\n\nWhy it matters: feature stores deliver reuse (build a feature once, use across many models), consistency (no skew), freshness (streaming features), and governance (lineage and access control) — accelerating delivery and improving reliability.\n\nUK context: feature reuse and lineage support model-governance evidence for the FCA/PRA, and on-prem/UK-region online stores address data-residency. Codeworth implements Feast (or Tecton for enterprise scale) so client features are point-in-time correct, reusable, and consistently served, eliminating training-serving skew.",
